    "result_text": "The Invoices page now has a \"Stage\" dropdown that narrows the list to one stage, such as only the ones you've sent. The acceptance test passes under `bin/e2e`.\n\n- **Server:** `GET /api/invoices` takes an optional `?status=DRAFT|SENT|PAID`. When it's given, the filtering happens in the database query, in `InvoiceRepository`, `InvoiceService.listAll(status)` and `AllInvoicesController`. Leaving it out returns every invoice, as before.\n- **Front end:** the dropdown in `invoices.ts` has the `data-testid` `invoice-status-filter` and defaults to \"All stages\". Changing it reloads the list from the server. If no invoices are at the chosen stage, the empty message says so (\"No invoices at the SENT stage.\") instead of \"No invoices yet.\"\n- **Database:** no migration was needed, because each invoice's stage is already stored. The request asked for one, but adding an empty migration would have done nothing.\n\nThe request also mentioned an OfficeFloor server, but this app's server is Spring Boot (as `CLAUDE.md` says), so I made the server change in Spring.\n\nAll existing `data-testid` values are unchanged.",
